      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of Y stenting using radiopaque stents for a bifurcation stenosis is described. Angiography and intravascular ultrasound demonstrate that in spite of optimal stent placement there is an area of the lesion that is not fully covered by the stents. This may predispose to subacute thrombosis and restenosis. This case illustrates a potential deficiency of this type of bifurcation stenting."},
